WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.971
Cybersecurity includes discovering exposed
assets,

2
00:00:03.051 --> 00:00:06.221
investigating weaknesses, assessing
software and infrastructure,

3
00:00:06.301 --> 00:00:08.611
building detections, and interpreting
evidence.

4
00:00:08.691 --> 00:00:12.560
These activities produce different
results: an inventory, a reproducible finding,

5
00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:14.735
a tested rule, or an intelligence
assessment.

6
00:00:14.815 --> 00:00:18.415
Artificial intelligence is useful when its
contribution advances one of those

7
00:00:18.495 --> 00:00:19.354
specific results.

8
00:00:19.434 --> 00:00:21.960
Assistance extends beyond asking a chatbot
questions.

9
00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:25.639
Models can organize discovery records,
explain code, draft analysis scripts,

10
00:00:25.719 --> 00:00:27.385
and correlate technical artifacts.

11
00:00:27.465 --> 00:00:30.581
Conventional tools still collect
measurements and execute checks.

12
00:00:30.661 --> 00:00:32.971
The relevant combination depends on the
activity:

13
00:00:33.051 --> 00:00:35.146
code paths matter in application
assessment,

14
00:00:35.226 --> 00:00:37.966
while event schemas and retained logs
matter in monitoring.

15
00:00:38.046 --> 00:00:40.464
This course surveys those professional
activities,

16
00:00:40.544 --> 00:00:43.714
including vulnerability research, cloud
and container assessment,

17
00:00:43.794 --> 00:00:46.158
incident response, and open-source
intelligence.

18
00:00:46.238 --> 00:00:49.569
AI-assisted threat modeling connects
architecture, trust boundaries,

19
00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:51.852
and plausible attack paths to design
decisions.

20
00:00:51.932 --> 00:00:55.585
AI-assisted risk management connects
security evidence with business impact,

21
00:00:55.665 --> 00:00:58.351
treatment options, accountable owners, and
review dates.

22
00:00:58.431 --> 00:01:01.977
Together, they help explain what could go
wrong and how an organization should

23
00:01:02.057 --> 00:01:02.487
respond.

24
00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:06.113
The aim is to identify where assistance
could reduce repetitive effort or make

25
00:01:06.193 --> 00:01:07.751
deeper investigation practical.

26
00:01:07.831 --> 00:01:10.464
Practitioners still verify evidence, test
assumptions,

27
00:01:10.544 --> 00:01:12.532
and make decisions within their authority.

28
00:01:12.612 --> 00:01:16.319
As you compare the activities, consider
which technical skills, source records,

29
00:01:16.399 --> 00:01:19.300
and business context would support useful
work in your own area.
